  "title": "A barber you’d trust with your life",
  "date": "08-09",
  "text": "1. \nA barber you’d trust with your life\nAllowing another man that close to your exposed neck with a blade every fortnight is, when you think about it, an act of extraordinary faith. And yet the greater risk isn’t mortal peril, it’s aesthetic negligence. The horror of being released back into society looking faintly… experimental. The right barber respects this. He considers the slope of your forehead, the ambition of your jawline, the inconvenient cowlick that has derailed lesser men. He works with what you’ve got, not against it.",
